# Git authorization

You may inspect the repo, edit local files, create a local branch, and run tests.

Do not execute commit, push, merge, rebase, cherry-pick, GitHub PR mutations,
tags, or releases without explicit user authorization for that operation.

Never force-push or run `git reset --hard` / `git clean -fd` unless the user
explicitly requests it.

Propose Conventional Commit messages and exact commands; the user runs them.
